Z||000000||88/2.8||02-05-2001||10:46 AM||||Well, first, my ignition module went bad, so i changed it, but now i have a timing problem. When i took the cap off to change the module i think i messed up the timing because the car is not as responsive as it used to be. i tried turning the cap and advancing the timing but it gets to a certain point and then starts to hit a tube and wont turn anymore.the car is still more sluggish than is used to be and it idles kind of rough PLEASE HELP!!!||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||02-05-2001||11:17 AM||||Are you sure that the distributor cap is in the slot correctly where the connectors are? What brand of ignition module did you get? It is not uncommon to buy and ignition module that is bad. Do you have the ECM pins shorted before you time it? If they aren't shorted, everytime you adjust the timing the computer will try to correct it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||02-05-2001||01:09 PM||||You need a timing light to check the timing correctly. If it is off and you can't get close enough then you can lift the distributor and move the gears over a tooth.||||reg||4
